    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The neighborhood’s historic Lincoln Theater, a key venue for African‑American jazz, remains a cultural landmark in Olde Towne East.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.experiencecolumbus.com/neighborhoods/near-east-side/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "OTENA, founded in 1975, steers preservation efforts and community zoning to protect Olde Towne East’s historic character.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.oldetowneeast.org/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Olde Towne East sits on a high ridge that was part of the original 1812 layout of Columbus, making it a natural early settlement spot.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Olde_Towne_East"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The area once hosted a carpet factory whose site was later cleaned after being found laced with arsenic and other chemicals.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Olde_Towne_East"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Gemüt Biergarten, a German‑style brewery housed in a historic firehouse, is a modern culinary highlight of Olde Towne East.",
